@startuml use-case
title Smart Campus - Study Room Booking\nUse-case diagram (revised)

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false

actor Student
actor Administrator

rectangle "Smart Campus Study Room Booking System" {
  usecase "View room availability" as UC_View
  usecase "Book room" as UC_Book
  usecase "Cancel own booking" as UC_Cancel
  usecase "Block room" as UC_Block
  usecase "Unblock room" as UC_Unblock
  usecase "Review room usage" as UC_Review
}

' Student goals: US-01, US-02, US-03
Student -- UC_View
Student -- UC_Book
Student -- UC_Cancel

' Administrator goals: US-04, US-05, US-06
UC_Block   -- Administrator
UC_Unblock -- Administrator
UC_Review  -- Administrator

note right of UC_Book
  US-01. Checked before the booking is created:
  R1 future start, 0 < duration <= 2 h
  R3 room not blocked
  R2 no overlap with an active booking of the
     same room; touching is allowed (A2)
  R4 on success the Student gets a confirmation -
     an outcome of Book room, not a separate goal
end note

note right of UC_Block
  US-04 / R3: stops NEW bookings only.
  Existing bookings are kept (A1).
end note

note right of UC_Cancel
  US-03: only the student who made the booking;
  the cancelled booking stops counting for R2.
end note
@enduml
